      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey quick question, im trying to run the numbers for a new CNC machine we just bought for the shop. how do i actually calculate the straight-line depreciation for it? i want to make sure i have the formula right for the year-end reports.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Straight-line depreciation is calculated by taking the cost of the CNC machine, subtracting the salvage value (what the machine will be worth after its useful life), and then dividing by the useful life of the machine in years. The formula looks like this: Depreciation Expense = (Cost - Salvage Value) / Useful Life. This will give you an annual depreciation expense. For your year-end reports, you just multiply that annual expense by the number of years that have passed.",
